    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0740" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg620"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">463.00 R 29/118: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washburn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-23T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>36. Logan’s B–732, August 7, 4 p.m.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d364-f1"/></p>
                <p>Inform Austrian Government that this Government has noted the action taken by the
                    Reparations Commission on August 7, and is prepared, within limits of Public
                    Resolution number 46, April 6, last,<anchor n="9" xml:id="d364-f2"/> to suspend
                    priorities to the extent necessary for realization of new Austrian Bank of
                    Issue.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d364-f1" n="8" xml:id="d364-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted in telegram from the Chargé in France, no. 311, Aug. 7, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d364-f2" n="9" xml:id="d364-f2-content">
                <p>Text quoted in note of Apr. 13, to the Austrian Chargé, <ref target="#pg617">p.
                        617</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
